# ERP Unite

A functional walkthrough for HSO business consultants.

<div class="byline">Functional consultant pack · feature-by-feature · configuration touchpoints</div>

---

<!-- _class: stat -->

<div class="number">5</div>

## end-to-end business flows

Statement-to-cash. Cash-to-GL. Accrual-to-AH. Split-intake-to-payable. Collections-to-write-off. **You will configure and demo all five.**

---

# The five flows you need to know

Every customer engagement returns to one of these. Learn them in order.

<div class="cols three">
<div class="card">

### 1. Statement → Cash
Carrier sends statement → Unite ingests → cash gets applied to the right invoices.

</div>
<div class="card">

### 2. Cash → GL
Applied cash flows through the AH integration → ledger posting.

</div>
<div class="card">

### 3. Accrual → AH
Month-end accruals computed by cost center → posted to AH as journals.

</div>
</div>

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### 4. Split Intake → Payable
Producer comp rules + product splits → CompensationActualSnapshot → payable transaction → AH.

</div>
<div class="card">

### 5. Collections → Write-off
Aging accruals → collections case → workflow approval → write-off journal → AH.

</div>
</div>

---

<!-- _class: section -->

# Flow 1 — Statement to Cash

The flagship. Lead every demo here.

---

# Step 1.1 — Statement Import

Brokers drop carrier statements into Unite. Two ways: single upload (`/Statements`) or bulk upload (`/StatementsBulkImport`).

- **Single upload** — pick a file, optionally pick a template, hit Upload
- **Bulk upload** — drop a folder; system fingerprints each file and matches to templates
- **Backfill mode** — for historical files; same pipeline, different processing-status flag
- **What gets created:** a `StatementHeader` shell + a `StatementFileFingerprint` row + blob storage entry

*Configuration touchpoint:* `StatementConfiguration` page. Provider filters, statement filter rules, AI prompt overrides.

---

# Step 1.2 — Template Matching

Every statement needs a template. Templates know "this carrier puts the customer name in column C, the gross amount in column F" — and they handle every transformation in between.

- **Auto-suggest by fingerprint** — Unite hashes the file structure and proposes templates that match
- **Auto-suggest by AI** — Mapping Studio offers Gemini-driven column mappings
- **Manual assignment** — user picks the template from the dropdown
- **Status lifecycle:** InProgress → Active → Archived
- **Versioning:** copy an active template to draft, edit, activate to replace

*Configuration touchpoint:* `StatementTemplateList` (`/StatementTemplateList/{All,InProgress,Blocked,Testing,Active}`) — filter by status, sort by use.

---

# Statement Studio — the AI authoring surface

![bg right:55%](screens/cashhub-mapping-studio.png)

Where new carrier formats get onboarded. Three-step wizard:

- **Step 1 — Upload** (the empty state shown here)
- **Step 2 — Show file** — PDF/Excel preview with overlays
- **Step 3 — Map fields** — Gemini suggestions, reviewer accepts

*The most-demoed screen in the product.*

---

# Step 1.3 — Mapping Studio (the AI bit)

This is where new carrier formats get onboarded. Open `/MappingStudio` with a draft template.

- **Step 1 — Upload** the carrier file
- **Step 2 — Show file** — Mapping Studio renders the PDF/Excel with overlays
- **Step 3 — Map fields** — click a column header, Gemini suggests a destination
- **Step 4 — Test extraction** — preview rows before committing
- **OCR regions** — for PDF tables not parsed by structure, region-select and OCR

*Configuration touchpoint:* `ExpressionBuilder` lets you type column transformations in Gemini-translated NL. "If column starts with 'P' it's premium, else it's fee" — becomes executable script.

---

# Step 1.4 — Cash Application Review

Once statements are extracted, the matching pipeline runs. Open `/CashApplicationReviewV4/{HeaderId}` to review.

- **Auto-matched lines** appear with their proposed `Product` + `Customer`
- **Unmatched lines** route to Reconcile Unmatched (`/cashapplication/reconcile/...`)
- **Manual match** creates a `MatchRule` for next time — the system learns
- **Approve / Unapprove** at line or header level — bulk actions in the toolbar
- **Split lines** for service-period allocation (parent + N children pattern)

*Configuration touchpoint:* `CashApplicationMatchRules` (`/CashApplicationMatchRules`) — see all learned rules, deactivate the noisy ones.

---

# Step 1.5 — Approve to Accounting Hub

Final step. Approved lines flow out via the AH integration.

- **Per-line approval** — line.IsApproved=true
- **Cascade** — approving a parent cascades to all split children
- **Header stats** roll up parent + standalone counts (children are display-only)
- **AH handoff** runs out-of-band via `CashApplicationToAHHandoff` function
- **Status tracking** in `ImportsStatistics` — every transfer is auditable

*Configuration touchpoint:* the AH integration blob containers + folder names — set per environment in `appsettings.json` `AzureStorage.Accounting`.

---

<!-- _class: section -->
<!-- _color: #00B294 -->

# Flow 2 — Accruals & Collections

Month-end. The piece every CFO loves.

---

# Statements list — staged for the workflow

![bg right:55%](screens/cashhub-statements-list.png)

Every statement received, on one screen.

- Stage chips: All / Ingesting / Processed / Deposit Matched / Cash Matching / Approved
- Assignment toggle: All / Assigned to me
- Gross/net totals roll up
- Per-row actions: Open, Configuration, Open in Statement Studio

---

# Cash Application headers — the queue

![bg right:55%](screens/cashhub-cash-applications.png)

The list of cash app headers waiting for review and approval.

- Filter by approval status
- Drill into Review &amp; Approve V4 for line-level workflow
- Header stats: approved count, requires-review count, no-match count
- Multi-header bulk approve from the toolbar

---

# Step 2.1 — Accruals Preview

Read-only dashboard. `/Accruals/Preview`.

- **By cost center × month** — every accruable product
- **Variance vs. prior month** — flagged with the magnitude
- **Drilldown** — click into a variance, see the product detail
- **Override-able** — but overrides go through Accrual Batches, not Preview

*Configuration touchpoint:* `AccrualConfiguration` (cost-center inclusion toggles) + `AccrualBrokerConfigs` (per-broker ignore flag).

---

# Step 2.2 — Accrual Batches

Where overrides + workflow live. `/Accruals/Batches`.

- **Create batch** — pick cost center + month, system computes lines
- **Edit lines** — override amount per line, document the reason
- **Submit** → `NotSubmitted → Submitted` workflow transition
- **Approve** → `Submitted → Approved` (separate permission)
- **Approved batches** flow out via `AccrualsOverrideToAHHandoff`

*Configuration touchpoint:* the workflow framework lives in shared. To change approval steps, you're editing `WorkflowService` + `WorkflowAuthorizationService` — not config.

---

# Step 2.3 — Collections Cases

For accruals that age. `/Collections/Cases`.

- **Multi-select aged lines** in Accrual Batch Lines detail → "Create Collections Case"
- **Snapshot** — at creation time, product fields are frozen onto `CollectionsCaseLine`
- **Actions** (past) and **Tasks** (future) recorded inline
- **Workflow approval** generates a write-off `JournalBatch` automatically
- **Audit trail** — every action, every status change, persisted

*Configuration touchpoint:* `WriteOffReasonCode` table — admin/DBA-managed today. Note `OpenQuestions.md` flags this as a productization decision.

---

<!-- _class: section -->
<!-- _color: #F1554B -->

# Flow 3 — Compensation & Split Intake

The CompHub side. Where producer pay actually happens.

---

# Step 3.1 — Producer Comp Rules

The rules that govern compensation. `/ProducerCompRules`.

- **One rule per producer × vertical × account type × renewal year**
- **VCP rates** — year 1, year 2/3 renewal, plus separate net/gross flags
- **Soft-delete** via `IsRuleActive` — rules are never hard-deleted (audit)
- **Effective dating** — rules carry an `EffectiveDate`; new rules supersede old

*Configuration touchpoint:* `Parties.razor` (`/parties/AllProducers`) for the producer master; comp rules link off the detail.

---

# Accrual Batches — month-end workflow

![bg right:55%](screens/cashhub-accruals-batches.png)

Cost-center × month batches with workflow approval.

- Workflow status pills at top
- Submitted by / approved by columns drive audit
- Drill into batch lines for per-line overrides
- Approved batches handoff to AH

---

# Collections Cases — non-invoiced worklist

![bg right:55%](screens/cashhub-collections-cases.png)

The aged-accrual investigation board.

- Created from Accrual Batch Lines multi-select
- Actions recorded with timestamps
- Workflow approval generates the write-off journal
- Closed cases preserve full audit trail

---

# Step 3.2 — Split Intake (SIF) — the heart of CompHub

How producers split commissions across themselves and cost centers.

- **Header** — broker, opportunity, vertical, effective date
- **Lines** — payee allocations (producer, %, account type, region)
- **Cost-center allocations** — sub-tab on the detail
- **Versioning** — every "request changes" on an approved header creates a new version (`SplitIntakeWorkflowActionHook`)
- **Audit log** — every field change is captured in `SplitIntakeChangeLog`

*Configuration touchpoint:* templates (`SplitIntakeHeaderTemplate`, `SplitIntakeLineTemplate`) for bulk SIF creation.

---

# Step 3.3 — SIF Coverage Audit

The "have we set up SIFs for every active product?" check.

- **Open `/SifCoverageAudit/{Mode}`** — pick coverage mode
- **System cross-references** Products vs. SplitIntakeHeaders
- **Shows uncovered products** — the gap
- **Direct link** to "Create SIF for this product"

*Configuration touchpoint:* `CreateSplitIntakeAdmin.razor` (`/Administration/CreateSplitIntake`) — admin bulk creation interface.

---

# Split Intake — the SIF list

![bg right:55%](screens/comphub-split-intake-list.png)

Every split intake header, by workflow status.

- Filter: All / My Tasks / My Team
- Versioning visible in the grid (latest vs. historical)
- Cost-center allocation on the detail
- Approval triggers compensation reprocessing

---

# Producer Comp Rules — the rate table

![bg right:55%](screens/comphub-producer-comp-rules.png)

The rates that drive every payable calculation.

- One rule per producer × product vertical × renewal year
- VCP year-1, year-2 renewal, year-3+ renewal
- Soft-delete (`IsRuleActive`) preserves history
- Effective dating supersedes old rules

---

# Step 3.4 — Compensation Actuals

The output. `/compensation-actuals`.

- **Batches** — periodic compensation runs, each with their own workflow
- **Lines** — per-producer payable amount
- **Invoice IDs** — auto-generated on Approved status via `CompensationBatchWorkflowActionHook`
- **Inbound from AH** — `ProducerCompActualsAHToPCHHandoff` pulls actuals from AH after invoices are paid
- **Outbound to AH** — `ProducerPayableTransactionToAHHandoff` sends approved lines to AH

*Configuration touchpoint:* `AccountingHubSendStatus` enum on the batch — tracks whether AH has acknowledged.

---

